// "Airbend [objects]" [CR#701.65a]: the actor exiles them, and "for each card
// exiled this way, for as long as it remains exiled, its owner may cast it by
// paying {2} rather than paying its mana cost." The reminder text reads
// "Exile it. While it's exiled, its owner may cast it for {2} rather than its
// mana cost." for one object and "Exile them. While each one is exiled, its
// owner may cast it for {2} rather than its mana cost." for several.
//
// Only the exile mentions the parameter: the exile makes the objects new
// objects, which the rest of the effect finds as what it moved
// [CR#400.7,400.7j], so every later mention is the anaphor `it` (§7, ruling
// 2026-10-08, "A moved referent is read back by anaphora"). The body is the
// singular reminder's. "It" agrees with one object only, so several airbended
// objects ("airbend up to two target creatures") are refused until the
// per-card loop below lands (`semantics-v2-per-member-handoff`).
KeywordAction(
    name: "airbend",
    params: [Subject],
    spelling: "airbend <Param(0)>",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "airbend",
        frame_set: Transitive,
    ),
    body: sequentially([
        exile(Param(0)),
        act(
            // STOP: one performer, the singular reminder's. The per-card
            // spelling, the plural reminder's "while each one is exiled",
            // loops over the cards exiled this way with `it` inside:
            // `doForEach(allOf(and([card, happenedTo(verbedEvent(exile,
            // relative(Object)), ThisWay)])), act(ownerOf(it), …it…))`. It
            // waits on `lean-drt-anaphora-refactor`: for one object each "it"
            // ties between the loop's card and the exiled object.
            ownerOf(it),
            establish(
                mayCastFrom(it, exileZone, PayingInstead(mana([2]))),
                forAsLongAs(matches(it, inZone(exileZone))),
            ),
        ),
    ]),
)
